# Precon project stack

All internal Precon apps share this infrastructure. See `docs/SETUP.md` for step-by-step provisioning.

## Platform

| Piece | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| **Next.js 16+ (App Router)** | Web framework — TypeScript required for new code |
| **Vercel** | Hosting, preview deployments, env vars |
| **Microsoft Entra ID** | Company login (Auth.js / next-auth) |
| **Neon Postgres (EU)** | Serverless Postgres — use pooled `DATABASE_URL` |

## Auth pattern

- Provider: Microsoft Entra ID (`AUTH_MICROSOFT_ENTRA_ID_*` env vars)
- Security groups gate access (e.g. `precon-<app>-users`, `precon-<app>-admins`)
- Enterprise app: **Assignment required** — only assigned groups can sign in
- Groups exposed via ID token optional claim
- Role checks in API routes and server components — never trust client-side flags

## Database pattern

```ts
// lib/db.ts
import { neon } from "@neondatabase/serverless";
export const sql = neon(process.env.DATABASE_URL!);
```

- Always use **pooled** `DATABASE_URL` in route handlers (hostname contains `-pooler`)
- Use `DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED` only for migrations
- Parameterized queries only — never string-concatenate SQL
- EU region (e.g. `aws-eu-central-1`) for Dutch users

## Environment variables

- Secrets live in Vercel + `.env.local` (never committed)
- Local: `npx vercel env pull .env.local`
- No `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix on secrets — only on truly public config
- Validate required env vars at startup (use `zod` or similar)

## Naming conventions

- Entra app registration: `Precon <App Name>`
- Security groups: `precon-<app-slug>-users`, `precon-<app-slug>-admins`
- Neon database: `<app-slug>` (kebab-case)
